{"name":"Sunday Best","hex":"#fcc9c7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"best","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["superlative form of good: most good.","Most; largest."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["superlative form of well: most well","To the most advantage; with the most success, cause, profit, benefit, or propriety."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/best"}],"entries":[{"title":"Christian clothing","blocks":[{"text":"Many Christians have followed certain dress codes during attendance at church. Customs have varied over time and among different Christian denominations. As with the Bible, the Church Fathers of Christianity taught modesty as a core principle guiding the clothing that Christians are to manufacture and wear."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christian_clothing","wikidata":"Q5110311"},{"title":"Sunday Best (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Sunday Best Recordings is a British music label, founded by DJ Rob da Bank and Sarah Bolshi in 2000."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunday_Best_(company)","wikidata":"Q7639339"},{"title":"Sunday Best (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Sunday Best is the fifth studio album by the American singer-songwriter Nick Jonas, released on February 6, 2026, through Republic Records. The album contains a sole guest appearance from his band the Jonas Brothers, which includes his older brothers Joe and Kevin Jonas. Production was handled by Ryan Daly, Tommy English, Jeremy Hatcher, James Amaradio, Kevin Farzad, Joel Little, Jeff Gitelman, and Matt Bronleewe."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c0/Sunday-Best-Nick-Jonas-cover.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunday_Best_(album)","wikidata":"Q137205879"},{"title":"Sunday","blocks":[{"text":"Sunday is the day of the week between Saturday and Monday. Sunday is a day of rest in most Western countries and a part of the weekend. In some Arab countries, Sunday is a weekday."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif/lossy-page1-330px-Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunday","wikidata":"Q132"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Kerkdienst_hhk_doornspijk.jpg/330px-Kerkdienst_hhk_doornspijk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Kerkdienst_hhk_doornspijk.jpg/330px-Kerkdienst_hhk_doornspijk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Christian headcovering and modesty being practiced in a Restored Reformed Church in Doornspijk, Gelderland (the Netherlands)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKerkdienst_hhk_doornspijk.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Pierre-Le-Moyne-De-l%27art-de-regner_MGG_0910.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sol Iustitiae (Sun of Righteousness), derived from the Judeo-Christian Bible, Malachi 4:2. By Albrecht Dürer, c. 1499/1500","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APierre-Le-Moyne-De-l'art-de-regner_MGG_0